.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt LINUXD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm linuxd
.Nd RavenBSD Linux personality server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar image
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
registers the
.Dq linux:
scheme, loads one static Linux executable from the
.Xr initfs 5
archive and starts it as a native RavenBSD process with the Linux personality.
The kernel delivers every Linux syscall of that process to the handler as a
.Dv CALL
packet carrying a
.Vt LinuxSyscallV1
request; the server answers with a
.Vt LinuxReplyV1
value that the kernel writes to the process's return register.
.Pp
An existing client that opens
.Dq linux:
blocks until the server acknowledges the open; the personality handler itself is
the scheme-server handle the server registered, so the server needs no self-open.
.Pp
The skeleton serves
.Cm write ,
.Cm exit_group ,
.Cm brk ,
.Cm mmap
(anonymous only),
.Cm getpid ,
.Cm uname ,
.Cm rt_sigprocmask
and
.Cm arch_prctl .
Anonymous
.Cm mmap
and
.Cm brk
come from two pre-mapped arenas
.Pq 1 MiB each ;
every other number returns
.Er ENOSYS
and is counted in the statistics the server prints before it exits.
.Pp
The default image path is
.Pa /hello ;
the optional
.Ar image
argument selects another path in the initfs.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The server exits 0 after the Linux process exits, and prints the dispatcher
statistics
.Pq per-syscall calls and errors, and the unimplemented hits .
A load failure exits 3, a failed personality switch 5, and a Linux process that
does not reach its first syscall within 20 seconds 1.
.Sh LIMITATIONS
The trap packet carries no process identity, so one server instance serves one
Linux process at a time.
.Cm arch_prctl
with
.Dv ARCH_SET_FS
returns
.Er ENOSYS
because the kernel has no per-thread FS base; a static musl program stops in
.Fn __init_tls
until that primitive exists.
There is no dynamic loader, no file descriptor table beyond stdio, and no
.Pa /proc .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr nulld 8
